        // which is always true for uint (except overflow which makes it false). Mutant checks > 
        // which would also fail only on overflow? Actually if balance + msg.value == 0 (both zero), 
        // original passes (0>=0), mutant fails (0>0 false). So the mutant rejects zero-value deposits.
        // The invariant: After Collect, the caller's balance should be such that a subsequent Put(0) succeeds.
        // For the reference, it always succeeds. For the mutant, it reverts if balance == 0 after Collect.
        // Thus the general rule: balance == 0 only after Collect if the call reverted (otherwise balance > 0).
        // Actually simpler: After any Collect that succeeds, the caller's balance is never 0.
        assertTrue(!success || balance > 0);
    }
